---
title: Carrot Cake Muffins
image: https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/carrot-cake-muffins-3sm-5.jpg
time required: 35 minutes
course: Breakfast
cook time: 20 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cuisine: American
servings: 14
nutrition:
  calories: 208 kcal
  fat: 9 g
  saturated fat: 7 g
  carbohydrates: 31 g
  sugar: 20 g
  protein: 2 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 162 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
source: https://www.lecremedelacrumb.com/carrot-cake-muffins/
---

Preheat oven to 350°F.

Line a #muffin tin{} with paper or silicone cupcake liners (or grease well with cooking spray).

In a #medium bowl{} whisk together @flour{1.5%cups}, @sugar{1%cup}, @cinnamon{1%teaspoon}, @baking soda{0.5%teaspoon}, @baking powder{0.5%teaspoon}, and @salt{0.5%teaspoon}.

In a #large bowl{} combine @vegetable oil{0.5%cups}, @brown sugar{1/3%cup}, @eggs{2%large}(at room temperature), and @vanilla extract{2%teaspoons} and mix well. 

Stir in @carrots{2%cups}(finely grated, not pre-shredded).

> We found this is about ~220g of carrots, or 5 medium / 2 large carrots. Personally, you can probably err a little more than even that.

Stir dry ingredients into wet ingredients until completely incorporated. Be careful not to over stir.

Fill muffin liners 2/3 full.

Bake in preheated oven for ~{20-22%minutes} until a toothpick inserted in the center of the muffins comes out clean. Cool for ~{5%minutes} before transferring to a cooling rack to continue cooling.

> Serve fresh or store in airtight container at room temperature up to 3 days, or in the fridge up to 2 weeks. Optional: reheat them in the microwave for about 15 seconds and spread a little butter/honey on top for the ultimate breakfast treat.